{
  "id": 197,
  "Specification": "Defines the transitive closure of a relation R (a set of ordered pairs) using five increasingly efficient definitions: TC via paths in Seq(S), TC1 via bounded sequences, TC2 via algebraic composition, TC3 via recursive squaring, TC4 implementing Warshall's algorithm, and TC5 representing relations as Boolean operators. Two ASSUMEs check the definitions agree.",
